# Environment variables for shahrul-portfolio
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development (Next.js loads
# `.env.local` automatically and it is git-ignored). In production, set
# these as real environment variables on your host (Vercel project settings,
# or the process manager / systemd unit / PM2 ecosystem file on a
# self-hosted VPS) — do not ship a `.env` file to production.
#
# IMPORTANT: any variable prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` is inlined into the
# client-side JavaScript bundle at build time and is visible to anyone who
# opens the site in a browser. Never put a secret behind a `NEXT_PUBLIC_`
# name. `RESEND_API_KEY` and `CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL` below are server-only and
# are read exclusively inside the `/api/contact` route handler
# (`src/app/api/contact/route.ts` -> `src/lib/email.ts`), which runs on the
# Node.js runtime and never ships to the browser. `NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_SRC`
# and `NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_DOMAIN` further below ARE `NEXT_PUBLIC_` and
# therefore visible in the client bundle — that is fine, since neither one
# is a secret (they are just a script URL and a site identifier).

# Resend (https://resend.com) API key used to send contact-form emails.
# Required to actually deliver messages submitted through /contact.
# Read in: src/lib/email.ts (sendContactEmail).
#
# If this is UNSET: the app still builds and runs fine (the Resend client is
# constructed lazily, only after this key is confirmed present). The contact
# API route returns HTTP 503 with the message "Email delivery is not
# configured on this deployment yet." instead of attempting to send, and in
# non-production environments the submission payload is logged to the
# server console for local debugging.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# The "From" address used on outgoing contact-form emails, e.g.
# "Portfolio Contact <contact@yourdomain.com>". Must be a sender/domain
# verified in your Resend account, or Resend will reject the send.
# Read in: src/lib/email.ts (sendContactEmail).
#
# Optional. If UNSET, falls back to Resend's shared sandbox sender
# "Portfolio Contact <onboarding@resend.dev>", which works for testing but
# is not suitable for production (low deliverability, not your domain).
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=

# Privacy-first analytics (brief: "Additional Features" #10 — no Google
# Analytics). Both are optional and read in src/components/analytics.tsx.
# The shape (a script `src` + a `data-domain` attribute) fits a cookieless,
# self-hostable analytics service such as Plausible or Umami — no vendor is
# hardcoded, and neither variable ships with a default.
#
# If EITHER is UNSET, analytics is disabled entirely: the component renders
# nothing and the site loads zero third-party scripts, exactly as it does
# today. Both are `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, so once set they are visible in the
# client bundle — that's expected and not a secret leak, since a script URL
# and a site domain aren't sensitive.

# The analytics provider's script URL, e.g.
# "https://analytics.example.com/script.js". Optional; leave blank to
# disable analytics.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_SRC=

# The site identifier the analytics provider expects in `data-domain`, e.g.
# "shahrulsaifuddin.com". Optional; leave blank to disable analytics.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_DOMAIN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not an environment variable, but related and easy to miss before deploying:
# `siteConfig.url` in `src/lib/site.ts` is currently a PLACEHOLDER domain
# (https://shahrulsaifuddin.com) used for canonical URLs, Open Graph/Twitter
# metadata, JSON-LD, sitemap.xml and robots.txt. Update it to the real
# production domain before deploying, or all of the above will point at the
# wrong host.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
